{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat outputs/repomix/2026-09-16-s8-r373-release.xml'","aggregated_output":"This file is a merged representation of a subset of the codebase, containing specifically included files, combined into a single document by Repomix.\n\n<file_summary>\nThis section contains a summary of this file.\n\n<purpose>\nThis file contains a packed representation of a subset of the repository's contents that is considered the most important context.\nIt is designed to be easily consumable by AI systems for analysis, code review,\nor other automated processes.\n</purpose>\n\n<file_format>\nThe content is organized as follows:\n1. This summary section\n2. Repository information\n3. Directory structure\n4. Repository files (if enabled)\n5. Multiple file entries, each consisting of:\n  - File path as an attribute\n  - Full contents of the file\n</file_format>\n\n<usage_guidelines>\n- This file should be treated as read-only. Any changes should be made to the\n  original repository files, not this packed version.\n- When processing this file, use the file path to distinguish\n  between different files in the repository.\n- Be aware that this file may contain sensitive information. Handle it with\n  the same level of security as you would the original repository.\n</usage_guidelines>\n\n<notes>\n- Some files may have been excluded based on .gitignore rules and Repomix's configuration\n- Binary files are not included in this packed representation. Please refer to the Repository Structure section for a complete list of file paths, including binary files\n- Only files matching these patterns are included: scripts/release-readiness.ts, scripts/release-readiness.test.ts, .github/workflows/release-train.yml, .github/workflows/security-scan.yml\n- Files matching patterns in .gitignore are excluded\n- Files matching default ignore patterns are excluded\n- Files are sorted by Git change count (files with more changes are at the bottom)\n</notes>\n\n</file_summary>\n\n<directory_structure>\n.github/\n  workflows/\n    release-train.yml\n    security-scan.yml\nscripts/\n  release-readiness.test.ts\n  release-readiness.ts\n</directory_structure>\n\n<files>\nThis section contains the contents of the repository's files.\n\n<file path=\".github/workflows/release-train.yml\">\nname: release-train\n# The ADR-0318 release train (R1–R4), reworked commit-addressable by ADR-0325. Publishing a\n# GitHub Release is THE trigger (R1) — its tag MUST target the merged version-PR commit\n# (version-pr.yml authored it; push-to-main CI proved it green). Everything rides it (R2):\n# registry tarball publish → registry Worker deploy → public-mirror sync → mirror npm publish →\n# site redeploy, in that order, each leg a dispatch of the existing workflow that already owns the\n# capability (no duplicated publish logic). Legs 1, 1b and 2 receive the release tag so they act on\n# EXACTLY the tagged bytes — one SHA anchors source, ledger, tarballs, edge catalog, mirror, and\n# evidence. Leg 1b was added 2026-07-31: leg 1 uploads bytes to R2 but the Worker inlines\n# registry/index.json at BUILD time, so without a Worker deploy a green train can leave the edge\n# resolving the previous release (observed on v2026.07.30). The readiness\n# job (R3, scripts/release-readiness.ts) runs first and any red check — including tag-not-on-main\n# — stops the train before it touches an external surface.\n#\n# STAYS DORMANT UNTIL ARMED: the propagation job runs only when the repo VARIABLE\n# RELEASE_TRAIN_ARMED is \"true\" (a variable, not a secret, so it can gate a job-level `if:`\n# directly — no guard-step dance needed). Until the operator sets it, a published release runs\n# readiness (useful signal) and skips propagation. The mirror + deploy legs additionally keep\n# their own inert-until-armed guards (MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN, RAILWAY_TOKEN), so arming the train\n# without arming those legs still no-ops them green. Leg 1 (registry publish) deliberately does\n# NOT no-op: with R2 keys unset it fails loud (a silent green \"publish\" would mark a release\n# done while buyers 404 on the tarballs).\n#\n# The retired per-push triggers: publish.yml (dry-run on every main push) and mirror-sync.yml\n# (snapshot per main push) no longer fire on push — the train is their scheduler now; both keep\n# workflow_dispatch as the manual lever.\non:\n  release:\n    types: [published]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: release-train\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  readiness:\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    timeout-minutes: 20\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      checks: read # readiness check 1 reads the check-runs API on the release SHA\n      pull-requests: read # `bun run sot` tracker-vs-reality reads PR states via `gh pr view`\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@0c5077e51419868618aeaa5fe8019c62421857d6 # v2.2.0\n        with:\n          bun-version: \"1.4.2\"\n      - run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\n      - name: release readiness (R3)\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          # env-indirect, never inlined in run: — a tag name may legally contain `$();|&`\n          # (github.sha is hex-safe but rides along for consistency).\n          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }}\n          RELEASE_SHA: ${{ github.sha }}\n        run: |\n          bun scripts/release-readiness.ts \\\n            --tag \"$RELEASE_TAG\" \\\n            --sha \"$RELEASE_SHA\"\n\n  propagate:\n    needs: readiness\n    # Dormant until the operator sets the RELEASE_TRAIN_ARMED repo variable to \"true\" (ADR-0318:\n    # the train ships dormant; W3 arming is an operator act). Skipped-when-unarmed keeps the\n    # workflow green.\n    if: vars.RELEASE_TRAIN_ARMED == 'true'\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    timeout-minutes: 90\n    environment: release # ADR-0327 rider 2 (definition-first; free-plan protection rules can't enforce yet)\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      actions: write # dispatch same-repo workflows (publish.yml, deploy-worker.yml, mirror-sync.yml, deploy-railway.yml)\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n      # Dispatch a workflow and block until its run concludes; fail the train on a red leg.\n      # `gh workflow run` returns no run id, so poll for the newest run created after dispatch\n      # (concurrency: single-operator repo + per-workflow concurrency groups make this safe).\n      - name: leg helper\n        run: |\n          cat > /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh <<'EOF'\n          #!/usr/bin/env bash\n          set -euo pipefail\n          repo=\"$1\"; workflow=\"$2\"; shift 2\n          before=\"$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')\"\n          gh workflow run \"$workflow\" -R \"$repo\" \"$@\"\n          run_id=\"\"\n          for _ in $(seq 1 30); do\n            sleep 10\n            run_id=\"$(gh run list -R \"$repo\" --workflow \"$workflow\" --created \">$before\" \\\n              --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId // empty')\"\n            [ -n \"$run_id\" ] && break\n          done\n          if [ -z \"$run_id\" ]; then echo \"::error::$repo/$workflow: dispatched run never appeared\"; exit 1; fi\n          echo \"watching $repo/$workflow run $run_id\"\n          gh run watch \"$run_id\" -R \"$repo\" --exit-status --interval 30\n          EOF\n          chmod +x /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh\n      - name: leg 1 — registry publish (verify + upload EXACTLY the tagged bytes, LIVE)\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n        run: |\n          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" publish.yml \\\n            -f dry_run=false -f tag=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n      # Leg 1 uploaded the tarball BYTES; this makes them RESOLVABLE. deploy-entry.ts inlines\n      # registry/index.json into the Worker bundle at build time, so without this leg the edge keeps\n      # serving its previously-baked catalog and `bun add @caisson/<pkg>` returns the last release —\n      # exactly what happened on v2026.07.30, where a fully green train left the site advertising an\n      # entry point the registry could not resolve. Numbered 1b, not 5, because the order is\n      # load-bearing: after the bytes exist (leg 1), before the site advertises them (leg 4).\n      - name: leg 1b — registry Worker deploy (bake the tagged index onto the live edge)\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n        run: |\n          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" deploy-worker.yml \\\n            -f ref=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n      - name: leg 2 — public mirror sync (exported at the release tag)\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n        run: |\n          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" mirror-sync.yml \\\n            -f ref=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n      - name: leg 3 — mirror npm publish (caisson-sh/caisson-oss)\n        # Pre-launch train rides skip the public npm leg (ADR-0329, amends 0325): MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN\n        # stopped being an inert-guard when mirror-sync armed it 2026-07-10, so this leg needs its\n        # own arming variable. Set RELEASE_NPM_MIRROR_ARMED=true at the ADR-0318 W3 public flip.\n        if: vars.RELEASE_NPM_MIRROR_ARMED == 'true'\n        env:\n          # MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN is the fine-grained PAT on caisson-sh/caisson-oss (contents +\n          # actions/workflows rw) — the same credential mirror-sync pushes with.\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN }}\n        run: /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh caisson-sh/caisson-oss publish.yml -f confirm=publish\n      - name: leg 4 — site redeploy\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n        # require_armed=true: an unarmed deploy leg must FAIL the train, not skip green. Found\n        # 2026-07-28 during v2026.07.27.1 — the train reported all legs green while the site kept\n        # serving the previous image, because RAILWAY_TOKEN is not a repo secret.\n        #\n        # ref=$RELEASE_TAG: without it, deploy-railway.yml's resolve-ref falls back to the\n        # dispatched run's github.sha — main HEAD at dispatch time, not the tag. Any merge to main\n        # during the multi-leg window would then bake a DIFFERENT registry/index.json into\n        # license/admin than leg 1b baked into the Worker, and the parity probe would red on a\n        # train that \"worked\". One SHA anchors every leg only if every leg is told which SHA.\n        run: |\n          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" deploy-railway.yml \\\n            -f require_armed=true -f ref=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n</file>\n\n<file path=\"scripts/release-readiness.test.ts\">\n// Guards the required-check SET itself, not any one gate's logic. REQUIRED_CHECKS is a bare string\n// list that release-readiness.ts compares against the GitHub check-runs API: a name here that no\n// workflow defines makes every release \"missing\" that check forever, and a job here that can be\n// skipped reds readiness on every release whose diff happened not to reach it. Both failures are\n// silent until a release is already in flight, which is the wrong time to find out.\n//\n// Parsed with Bun.YAML, not regex. A first pass matched job KEYS with `^ {2}<name>:` and grepped\n// for a 4-space `paths:`; the SHIP review defeated it three ways that this repo could plausibly\n// produce — a `needs: changes` + `if: needs.changes.outputs.x` gate (quality.yml already has that\n// `changes` job), a `paths:` at 6-space indent under a nested `on:`, and flow-style\n// `push: { paths: [...] }`. A text heuristic over YAML is the wrong tool when a parser is in hand.\nimport {\n  mkdtempSync,\n  mkdirSync,\n  readdirSync,\n  readFileSync,\n  rmSync,\n  writeFileSync,\n} from \"node:fs\";\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\nimport { execFileSync, spawnSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { dirname, join } from \"node:path\";\n\nimport { afterAll, describe, expect, test } from \"bun:test\";\n\nimport {\n  checkChecklist,\n  auditArtifactIsValid,\n  auditSuccessorIsValid,\n  ATTESTATION_ONLY_PATHS,\n  REQUIRED_CHECKS,\n} from \"./release-readiness.ts\";\n\ndescribe(\"R4 audit attestation\", () => {\n  const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), \"caisson-r4-\"));\n  afterAll(() => rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n  function git(repo: string, ...args: string[]): string {\n    return execFileSync(\"git\", args, {\n      cwd: repo,\n      env: {\n        ...process.env,\n        GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL: \"/dev/null\",\n        GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM: \"1\",\n      },\n      stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n    })\n      .toString()\n      .trim();\n  }\n  function scratch(): string {\n    const repo = mkdtempSync(join(dir, \"repo-\"));\n    git(repo, \"init\", \"--quiet\");\n    git(repo, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"R4 lifecycle fixture\");\n    git(repo, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"r4@example.invalid\");\n    writeFileSync(join(repo, \"product.ts\"), \"export const version = 1;\\n\");\n    commit(repo);\n    git(repo, \"tag\", \"v2026.08.18\");\n    writeFileSync(join(repo, \"product.ts\"), \"export const version = 2;\\n\");\n    commit(repo);\n    return repo;\n  }\n  function commit(repo: string): string {\n    git(repo, \"add\", \".\");\n    git(repo, \"commit\", \"--quiet\", \"-m\", \"test: lifecycle fixture\");\n    return git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\");\n  }\n  const fixtureRepo = scratch();\n  const binding = {\n    base: \"v2026.08.18\",\n    tag: \"v2026.09.16\",\n    reviewed_sha: git(fixtureRepo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"),\n  };\n  const clean = {\n    schema_version: 2,\n    ...binding,\n    status: \"clean\",\n    critical: 0,\n    reviewed_scope: [\"scripts/release-readiness.ts\"],\n    reviewers: [\n      {\n        role: \"code_review\",\n        identity: \"gw-code-reviewer\",\n        reviewed_at: \"2026-09-16T02:37:11Z\",\n      },\n      {\n        role: \"security_audit\",\n        identity: \"gw-security-auditor\",\n        reviewed_at: \"2026-09-16T02:37:11Z\",\n      },\n    ],\n  };\n  function fixture(text: string): string {\n    const path = join(dir, `${crypto.randomUUID()}.md`);\n    writeFileSync(path, text);\n    return path;\n  }\n  const document = (value: unknown) =>\n    `---\\n${JSON.stringify(value)}\\n---\\n# Audit\\n`;\n\n  function attestation(repo: string, reviewedSha: string): void {\n    mkdirSync(join(repo, \"outputs/audit\"), { recursive: true });\n    mkdirSync(join(repo, \"docs/releases\"), { recursive: true });\n    writeFileSync(\n      join(repo, `outputs/audit/release-audit-${binding.tag}.md`),\n      document({ ...clean, reviewed_sha: reviewedSha }),\n    );\n    writeFileSync(\n      join(repo, `docs/releases/${binding.tag}-checklist.md`),\n      \"- [x] fixture\\n\",\n    );\n  }\n\n  test(\"R4 real Git lifecycle accepts review A then attestation-only B\", () => {\n    const repo = scratch();\n    const a = git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\");\n    attestation(repo, a);\n    const b = commit(repo);\n    expect(a).not.toBe(b);\n    expect(auditSuccessorIsValid(repo, binding.tag, b)).toBe(true);\n    // Working-tree tampering cannot replace the committed attestation.\n    attestation(repo, git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD^\"));\n    writeFileSync(\n      join(repo, `outputs/audit/release-audit-${binding.tag}.md`),\n      \"invalid\",\n    );\n    expect(auditSuccessorIsValid(repo, binding.tag, b)).toBe(true);\n  });\n  test(\"R373 rejects committed audit with leading newline before frontmatter\", () => {\n    const repo = scratch();\n    attestation(repo, git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"));\n    const path = join(repo, `outputs/audit/release-audit-${binding.tag}.md`);\n    writeFileSync(path, `\\n${readFileSync(path, \"utf8\")}`);\n    const candidate = commit(repo);\n    // A clean working copy must not rescue malformed committed bytes either.\n    writeFileSync(path, readFileSync(path, \"utf8\").trimStart());\n    expect(auditSuccessorIsValid(repo, binding.tag, candidate)).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  test(\"R373 accepts committed complete checklist despite incomplete dirty copy\", () => {\n    const repo = scratch();\n    attestation(repo, git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"));\n    const candidate = commit(repo);\n    writeFileSync(\n      join(repo, `docs/releases/${binding.tag}-checklist.md`),\n      \"- [ ] dirty copy\\n\",\n    );\n    expect(checkChecklist(binding.tag, candidate, repo)).toBe(true);\n  });\n  test(\"R373 rejects checklist absent from candidate despite complete working copy\", () => {\n    const repo = scratch();\n    const candidate = git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\");\n    attestation(repo, candidate);\n    expect(checkChecklist(binding.tag, candidate, repo)).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  test(\"R373 rejects committed incomplete checklist despite completed dirty copy\", () => {\n    const repo = scratch();\n    attestation(repo, git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"));\n    const path = join(repo, `docs/releases/${binding.tag}-checklist.md`);\n    writeFileSync(path, \"- [ ] live evidence pending\\n\");\n    const candidate = commit(repo);\n    writeFileSync(path, \"- [x] live evidence complete\\n\");\n    expect(auditSuccessorIsValid(repo, binding.tag, candidate)).toBe(true);\n    expect(checkChecklist(binding.tag, candidate, repo)).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  test.each([\n    \"product.ts\",\n    \"outputs/audit/unreviewed.md\",\n    \"docs/releases/other-checklist.md\",\n    \" outputs/audit/other.md\",\n  ])(\"R4 real Git lifecycle rejects unreviewed successor path %s\", (path) => {\n    const repo = scratch();\n    const a = git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\");\n    attestation(repo, a);\n    mkdirSync(dirname(join(repo, path)), { recursive: true });\n    writeFileSync(join(repo, path), \"unreviewed product or policy byte\\n\");\n    const b = commit(repo);\n    expect(auditSuccessorIsValid(repo, binding.tag, b)).toBe(false);\n  });\n  test(\"R4 real Git lifecycle rejects an audit naming C instead of parent A\", () => {\n    const repo = scratch();\n    const a = git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\");\n    // C is a real distinct existing commit, not an invented forty-character fixture.\n    const c = git(repo, \"rev-parse\", `${a}^`);\n    attestation(repo, c);\n    const b = commit(repo);\n    expect(auditSuccessorIsValid(repo, binding.tag, b)).toBe(false);\n  });\n  test(\"R4 attestation allowlist names exactly the audit and checklist\", () => {\n    expect(ATTESTATION_ONLY_PATHS).toEqual([\n      \"outputs/audit/release-audit-{tag}.md\",\n      \"docs/releases/{tag}-checklist.md\",\n    ]);\n  });\n\n  test(\"R4 rejects an existing empty audit instead of accepting its filename\", () => {\n    expect(auditArtifactIsValid(fixture(\"\"), binding)).toBe(false);\n  });\n  test(\"R4 accepts a clean audit bound to the exact base, tag and reviewed parent SHA\", () => {\n    expect(auditArtifactIsValid(fixture(document(clean)), binding)).toBe(true);\n  });\n  test.each([\n    [\"failed verdict\", { status: \"issues_found\" }],\n    [\"blocking finding\", { critical: 1 }],\n    [\"wrong SHA\", { reviewed_sha: git(fixtureRepo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD^\") }],\n    [\"wrong base\", { base: \"v2026.07.30\" }],\n    [\"wrong tag\", { tag: \"v2026.09.17\" }],\n    [\"empty scope\", { reviewed_scope: [] }],\n    [\"blank scope\", { reviewed_scope: [\"  \"] }],\n    [\"no reviewers\", { reviewers: [] }],\n    [\n      \"duplicate roles\",\n      { reviewers: [clean.reviewers[0], clean.reviewers[0]] },\n    ],\n    [\n      \"blank identity\",\n      {\n        reviewers: [\n          { ...clean.reviewers[0], identity: \" \" },\n          clean.reviewers[1],\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n    [\n      \"invalid timestamp\",\n      {\n        reviewers: [\n          { ...clean.reviewers[0], reviewed_at: \"yesterday\" },\n          clean.reviewers[1],\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n    [\"unknown metadata\", { bypass: true }],\n  ] as const)(\"R4 rejects %s\", (_label, patch) => {\n    expect(\n      auditArtifactIsValid(fixture(document({ ...clean, ...patch })), binding),\n    ).toBe(false);\n  });\n  test(\"R4 fails closed for absent, malformed and prose-only artifacts\", () => {\n    expect(auditArtifactIsValid(join(dir, \"absent.md\"), binding)).toBe(false);\n    expect(auditArtifactIsValid(fixture(\"---\\n[invalid\\n---\\n\"), binding)).toBe(\n      false,\n    );\n    expect(\n      auditArtifactIsValid(fixture(\"Reviewed and approved\"), binding),\n    ).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\nconst WORKFLOWS_DIR = join(import.meta.dir, \"..\", \".github\", \"workflows\");\n\n/** The ONE `if:` a required job may carry — the CAISSON-96 draft guard, per ci.yml's header. */\nconst DRAFT_GUARD =\n  \"github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\";\n\ninterface Job {\n  name?: string;\n  if?: string;\n  needs?: string | string[];\n  \"continue-on-error\"?: boolean;\n  steps?: {\n    name?: string;\n    run?: string;\n    env?: Record<string, string>;\n    if?: string;\n    \"continue-on-error\"?: boolean;\n  }[];\n}\ninterface Trigger {\n  paths?: string[];\n  \"paths-ignore\"?: string[];\n}\ninterface Workflow {\n  on?: Record<string, Trigger | null>;\n  true?: Record<string, Trigger | null>; // YAML 1.1: a bare `on:` key parses as boolean true\n  jobs?: Record<string, Job>;\n}\n\ninterface Found {\n  file: string;\n  key: string;\n  job: Job;\n  triggers: Record<string, Trigger | null>;\n}\n\n/** Parse every workflow once, and index by the check-run NAME each job reports under — which is\n *  `name:` when present and the job key otherwise. release-readiness.ts matches on that reported\n *  name, so indexing by job key alone would go green while every release reported it missing. */\nconst unparsable: string[] = [];\n\nfunction jobsByReportedName(): Map<string, Found> {\n  const found = new Map<string, Found>();\n  for (const file of readdirSync(WORKFLOWS_DIR).filter(\n    (f) => f.endsWith(\".yml\") || f.endsWith(\".yaml\"),\n  )) {\n    let wf: Workflow;\n    try {\n      wf = Bun.YAML.parse(\n        readFileSync(join(WORKFLOWS_DIR, file), \"utf8\"),\n      ) as Workflow;\n    } catch (err) {\n      // Collected, not thrown. A parse error at module scope takes the whole suite down as\n      // \"0 pass / 0 fail\" — technically non-zero, but it reads as \"no tests ran\" rather than\n      // \"this workflow is malformed\", and it hides every other check in this file.\n      unparsable.push(`${file}: ${String(err)}`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    const triggers = wf.on ?? wf.true ?? {};\n    for (const [key, job] of Object.entries(wf.jobs ?? {})) {\n      found.set(job.name ?? key, { file, key, job, triggers });\n    }\n  }\n  return found;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"REQUIRED_CHECKS — the release-readiness gate's own input\", () => {\n  const byName = jobsByReportedName();\n\n  test(\"every workflow file parses — a throw here would blank the whole suite\", () => {\n    expect(unparsable).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  test(\"the set is non-empty, deduplicated, and at full strength\", () => {\n    // Guard the guard: a floor below the real size lets one silently drop out.\n    expect(REQUIRED_CHECKS.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(7);\n    expect(new Set(REQUIRED_CHECKS).size).toBe(REQUIRED_CHECKS.length);\n    // And the parse itself must have found something, or every check below is vacuous.\n    expect(byName.size).toBeGreaterThan(10);\n  });\n\n  test(\"every required check is a job some workflow actually reports under that name\", () => {\n    expect(REQUIRED_CHECKS.filter((name) => !byName.has(name))).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  test(\"no required check is path-scoped — a skipped check never reports and reads as missing\", () => {\n    // ci.yml's header states the rule from the PR side (a path-skipped required job never reports\n    // and the PR blocks forever); release-readiness.ts enforces it from the release side, where a\n    // check with zero runs lands in `missing`. Same constraint, both directions.\n    const scoped = REQUIRED_CHECKS.flatMap((name) => {\n      const hit = byName.get(name);\n      if (!hit) return [];\n      return Object.entries(hit.triggers)\n        .filter(([, t]) => t?.paths ?? t?.[\"paths-ignore\"])\n        .map(([event]) => `${name} (${hit.file}, on.${event})`);\n    });\n    expect(scoped).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  test(\"no required check is conditionally skippable — only the CAISSON-96 draft guard is allowed\", () => {\n    // The other way a required job silently stops reporting: a job-level `if:` or a `needs:` on a\n    // path-filter job. quality.yml already has a `changes` job of exactly that shape, so this is a\n    // pattern the repo can produce, not a hypothetical.\n    const conditional = REQUIRED_CHECKS.flatMap((name) => {\n      // The fail-closed aggregate is tested structurally and behaviorally below.\n      if (name === \"runtime-images-gate\") return [];\n      const hit = byName.get(name);\n      if (!hit) return [];\n      const reasons: string[] = [];\n      if (hit.job.if !== undefined && hit.job.if.trim() !== DRAFT_GUARD) {\n        reasons.push(`if: ${hit.job.if}`);\n      }\n      if (hit.job.needs !== undefined) {\n        reasons.push(`needs: ${String(hit.job.needs)}`);\n      }\n      return reasons.map((r) => `${name} (${hit.file}) — ${r}`);\n    });\n    expect(conditional).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  test(\"support-bot is in the set — ADR-0414 promoted it before automating its deploy\", () => {\n    // Pinned by name, not just by the structural rules above: the promotion is the whole reason\n    // deploy-railway.yml is allowed to ship this service automatically. Dropping it back to\n    // advisory silently restores \"a red bot deploys anyway\", which no structural check would catch.\n    expect(REQUIRED_CHECKS).toContain(\"support-bot\");\n    expect(byName.get(\"support-bot\")?.file).toBe(\"support-bot.yml\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"runtime images aggregate is required by release readiness\", () => {\n    expect(REQUIRED_CHECKS).toContain(\"runtime-images-gate\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"runtime aggregate always consumes the selector and complete matrix\", () => {\n    const hit = byName.get(\"runtime-images-gate\");\n    expect(hit?.file).toBe(\"security-scan.yml\");\n    expect(hit?.job.if).toBe(\"always()\");\n    expect(hit?.job.needs).toEqual([\"runtime-select\", \"runtime-images\"]);\n    expect(hit?.job[\"continue-on-error\"]).not.toBe(true);\n    expect(hit?.job.steps).toHaveLength(1);\n    const step = hit?.job.steps?.[0];\n    expect(step?.if).toBeUndefined();\n    expect(step?.[\"continue-on-error\"]).not.toBe(true);\n    expect(step?.env).toEqual({\n      SELECT_RESULT: \"${{ needs.runtime-select.result }}\",\n      MATRIX_RESULT: \"${{ needs.runtime-images.result }}\",\n    });\n  });\n\n  function aggregate(select: string, matrix: string): number | null {\n    const script = byName.get(\"runtime-images-gate\")?.job.steps?.[0]?.run;\n    if (!script) throw new Error(\"runtime aggregate script missing\");\n    // Execute the actual workflow gate with synthetic outcomes; no scanners or credentials.\n    return spawnSync(\"bash\", [\"-c\", script], {\n      env: {\n        PATH: process.env.PATH,\n        SELECT_RESULT: select,\n        MATRIX_RESULT: matrix,\n      },\n    }).status;\n  }\n\n  test(\"runtime aggregate rejects a failed matrix member\", () => {\n    expect(aggregate(\"success\", \"failure\")).toBe(1);\n  });\n\n  test(\"runtime aggregate is green only when both dependencies succeed\", () => {\n    for (const select of [\"success\", \"failure\", \"cancelled\", \"skipped\", \"\"]) {\n      for (const matrix of [\"success\", \"failure\", \"cancelled\", \"skipped\", \"\"]) {\n        expect(aggregate(select, matrix)).toBe(\n          select === \"success\" && matrix === \"success\" ? 0 : 1,\n        );\n      }\n    }\n  });\n});\n</file>\n\n<file path=\"scripts/release-readiness.ts\">\n#!/usr/bin/env bun\n/**\n * release-readiness.ts — the ADR-0318 R3 gate. Every check must be GREEN before the release\n * train's propagation legs run; any red exits nonzero and the train stops before touching an\n * external surface. Run by .github/workflows/release-train.yml on the release SHA, and locally:\n *\n *   bun scripts/release-readiness.ts --tag v2026.07.30 [--sha <sha>] [--local]\n *\n * Checks (R3, locked; #0 added by ADR-0325):\n *   0. Release SHA on main — the tag targets a commit that is an ancestor of origin/main (the\n *      merged version-PR commit; a tag cut on a stray branch must never train).\n *   0b. Release tag signed (ADR-0382) — `git tag -v` verifies the tag against the allowed-signers\n *      file. ADVISORY for now: tags cut before the lock are unsigned and cannot become signed.\n *   1. CI green on the release SHA — all seven required checks, including the source security\n *      layer, support-bot and the R359 runtime-images-gate aggregate, completed successfully.\n *   2. Changesets drained — no pending .changeset/*.md (the version PR consumed them —\n *      version-pr.yml, ADR-0325; never a feature-branch or tag-path act).\n *   3. CHANGELOGs written — every non-private workspace package's CHANGELOG.md leads with its\n *      package.json version.\n *   4. `bun run sot` green — the SoT drift tool (ADR-ceiling parity, frontmatter/docs freshness,\n *      archive integrity, tracker-vs-PR reality, changeset preflight). Doubles as the R3\n *      docs-freshness check.\n *   4b. Registry coverage invariants (CAISSON-85/86) — every module's `latest` has a tarball row\n *      (hard), no advertised version outside the frozen pre-sidecar backlog is rowless, and every\n *      served member pin resolves served+tarball-backed (advertise-follows-upload, static half).\n *   5. R4 audit artifact on file — outputs/audit/release-audit-<tag>.md (the fresh full\n *      SHIP-audit-lane review of the cumulative diff since the last release tag).\n *   6. Per-release checklist complete — docs/releases/<tag>-checklist.md exists with ZERO\n *      unchecked boxes (the human items: marketing surfaces, announcement, live-leg attestations).\n *   7. (--local only) the live-hybrid retrieval golden leg — services/docs `bun run test:live`\n *      with real keys (Kickoff-M picker 2026-07-10: this leg gates at release readiness, not PR\n *      CI). In the train (no keys) the checklist attestation (#6) carries it instead.\n */\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { existsSync, readdirSync, readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join, resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { checkRegistryCoverage } from \"../registry/scripts/coverage-invariants\";\n\nconst REPO = resolve(import.meta.dir, \"..\");\nexport const REQUIRED_CHECKS = [\n  \"check\",\n  \"standards-gate\",\n  \"registry-index\",\n  \"oscal-conformance\",\n  // ADR-0327 scan-gate flip (CAISSON-95): the deterministic security layer joins the required\n  // set once its installers are pinned — which landed in the same change as this line.\n  \"deterministic\",\n  // ADR-0414: the Python gate for services/support-bot, promoted out of advisory in the same\n  // change that gave that service an automated Railway deploy. Its paths filter was removed in\n  // the same commit — this list treats a check that never reported as `missing`, so a\n  // path-scoped required check would red readiness on every release that did not touch the bot.\n  \"support-bot\",\n  // R359 / CR-05: source scans cannot stand in for the enforcing runtime-image matrix.\n  \"runtime-images-gate\",\n] as const;\n\ninterface Args {\n  tag: string;\n  sha: string;\n  local: boolean;\n}\n\nfunction parseArgs(argv: readonly string[]): Args {\n  let tag = \"\";\n  let sha = \"\";\n  let local = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {\n    const a = argv[i];\n    if (a === \"--tag\") tag = argv[++i] ?? \"\";\n    else if (a === \"--sha\") sha = argv[++i] ?? \"\";\n    else if (a === \"--local\") local = true;\n  }\n  if (!tag) {\n    console.error(\"FATAL: --tag <release-tag> is required\");\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n  if (!sha) {\n    sha = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], { cwd: REPO })\n      .toString()\n      .trim();\n  }\n  return { tag, sha, local };\n}\n\ntype CheckResult = { name: string; ok: boolean; detail: string };\nconst results: CheckResult[] = [];\nfunction record(name: string, ok: boolean, detail: string): void {\n  results.push({ name, ok, detail });\n  console.log(`${ok ? \"  ✓\" : \"  ✗\"} ${name} — ${detail}`);\n}\n\nfunction run(cmd: string, args: readonly string[], cwd = REPO): string {\n  return execFileSync(cmd, [...args], {\n    cwd,\n    stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n  })\n    .toString()\n    .trim();\n}\n\n/** Blob contents are parser input: preserve every byte, including leading whitespace. */\nfunction readGitBlob(repo: string, sha: string, path: string): string {\n  return execFileSync(\"git\", [\"show\", `${sha}:${path}`], {\n    cwd: repo,\n    stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n  }).toString(\"utf8\");\n}\n\n// --- 0. release SHA on main (ADR-0325) -----------------------------------------------------------\nfunction checkTagOnMain(sha: string): void {\n  try {\n    // In CI the checkout is at the tag with full history; locally origin/main may be stale —\n    // refresh it quietly, tolerating offline runs (merge-base still answers from local refs).\n    try {\n      run(\"git\", [\"fetch\", \"origin\", \"main\", \"--quiet\"]);\n    } catch {\n      /* offline — check against the local origin/main ref */\n    }\n    run(\"git\", [\"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", sha, \"origin/main\"]);\n    record(\n      \"release SHA on main\",\n      true,\n      `${sha.slice(0, 8)} is an ancestor of origin/main`,\n    );\n  } catch {\n    record(\n      \"release SHA on main\",\n      false,\n      `${sha.slice(0, 8)} is NOT on origin/main — the tag must target the merged version-PR commit`,\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n// --- 0b. release tag is signed (ADR-0382) -------------------------------------------------------\n// An annotated tag says WHO claims a release; a signed one proves it. Without a signature anyone\n// with push access can move or forge a tag onto a different commit and every downstream leg — the\n// registry publish, the mirror sync, the fleet redeploy — trusts it, because each of them resolves\n// the tag rather than a SHA. `git tag -v` verifies against the allowed-signers file; it fails on an\n// unsigned tag, an unknown signer, and a signature that does not match the tag's bytes.\n//\n// Tags cut before the signing lock are unsigned and cannot retroactively become signed, so this is\n// a WARNING here rather than a hard gate: it reports honestly on every release without failing the\n// train on history it cannot change. Promote it to a blocking check once the first signed tag has\n// trained end to end (that flip is a one-word change: `record(..., ok, ...)`).\nfunction checkTagSigned(tag: string): void {\n  try {\n    run(\"git\", [\"tag\", \"-v\", tag]);\n    record(\"release tag signed\", true, `${tag} carries a valid signature`);\n  } catch {\n    // Not fatal — see above. Surfaced so an unsigned tag is a visible choice, never an oversight.\n    console.log(\n      `  ! release tag signed — ${tag} is UNSIGNED or its signer is not in the allowed-signers file (advisory; see docs/ops/release-tag-signing.md)`,\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n// --- 1. CI green on the release SHA -------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction checkCi(sha: string): void {\n  try {\n    const raw = run(\"gh\", [\n      \"api\",\n      `repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/${sha}/check-runs`,\n      \"--paginate\",\n      \"-q\",\n      \"[.check_runs[] | {name, status, conclusion}]\",\n    ]);\n    // --paginate emits one JSON array per page; normalize to a single list.\n    const runs = raw\n      .split(\"\\n\")\n      .filter(Boolean)\n      .flatMap(\n        (line) =>\n          JSON.parse(line) as {\n            name: string;\n            status: string;\n            conclusion: string | null;\n          }[],\n      );\n    const missing: string[] = [];\n    const red: string[] = [];\n    for (const required of REQUIRED_CHECKS) {\n      const match = runs.filter((r) => r.name === required);\n      if (match.length === 0) {\n        missing.push(required);\n        continue;\n      }\n      // A check re-run replaces its predecessor in the API answer set; any green instance passes.\n      if (\n        !match.some(\n          (r) => r.status === \"completed\" && r.conclusion === \"success\",\n        )\n      )\n        red.push(required);\n    }\n    const ok = missing.length === 0 && red.length === 0;\n    record(\n      \"CI green on release SHA\",\n      ok,\n      ok\n        ? `all ${String(REQUIRED_CHECKS.length)} required checks green at ${sha.slice(0, 8)}`\n        : `missing: [${missing.join(\", \")}] red: [${red.join(\", \")}]`,\n    );\n  } catch (err) {\n    record(\"CI green on release SHA\", false, `gh api failed: ${String(err)}`);\n  }\n}\n\n// --- 2. changesets drained -----------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction checkChangesetsDrained(): void {\n  const pending = readdirSync(join(REPO, \".changeset\")).filter(\n    (f) => f.endsWith(\".md\") && f !== \"README.md\",\n  );\n  record(\n    \"changesets drained\",\n    pending.length === 0,\n    pending.length === 0\n      ? \"no pending changesets\"\n      : `${String(pending.length)} pending (version cut not consumed): ${pending.slice(0, 5).join(\", \")}${pending.length > 5 ? \", …\" : \"\"}`,\n  );\n}\n\n// --- 3. CHANGELOGs written -----------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction checkChangelogs(): void {\n  const bad: string[] = [];\n  for (const group of [\"packages\", \"tooling\"]) {\n    const base = join(REPO, group);\n    if (!existsSync(base)) continue;\n    for (const slug of readdirSync(base)) {\n      const pj = join(base, slug, \"package.json\");\n      if (!existsSync(pj)) continue;\n      const pkg = JSON.parse(readFileSync(pj, \"utf8\")) as {\n        name: string;\n        version?: string;\n        private?: boolean;\n      };\n      if (pkg.private || !pkg.version) continue;\n      const changelog = join(base, slug, \"CHANGELOG.md\");\n      if (!existsSync(changelog)) {\n        bad.push(`${pkg.name} (no CHANGELOG.md)`);\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (!readFileSync(changelog, \"utf8\").includes(`## ${pkg.version}`))\n        bad.push(`${pkg.name} (no ## ${pkg.version} entry)`);\n    }\n  }\n  record(\n    \"CHANGELOGs written\",\n    bad.length === 0,\n    bad.length === 0\n      ? \"every versioned package's CHANGELOG leads with its current version\"\n      : bad.slice(0, 5).join(\"; \") + (bad.length > 5 ? \"; …\" : \"\"),\n  );\n}\n\n// --- 4. sot green (doubles as docs freshness) ----------------------------------------------------\nfunction checkSot(): void {\n  try {\n    run(\"bun\", [\"run\", \"sot\"]);\n    record(\"bun run sot\", true, \"SoT drift tool green (incl. docs freshness)\");\n  } catch (err) {\n    // Surface the captured drift report — a CI readiness red must not be blind (first ride:\n    // the only failure signal was this one-liner while sot's own output was swallowed).\n    const e = err as { stdout?: Buffer | string; stderr?: Buffer | string };\n    for (const chunk of [e.stdout, e.stderr]) {\n      const text = chunk?.toString().trim();\n      if (text) console.error(text);\n    }\n    record(\"bun run sot\", false, \"sot check failed — drift report above\");\n  }\n}\n\n// --- 4b. registry coverage invariants (CAISSON-85/86) --------------------------------------------\nfunction checkRegistryCoverageGate(): void {\n  // Static advertise-follows-upload proof: every module's latest has a tarball row (hard), no\n  // advertised version outside the frozen pre-sidecar backlog is rowless, and every served member\n  // pin resolves served+tarball-backed. Same invariants the registry-index CI job enforces via\n  // coverage-invariants.test.ts — re-run here so the train's readiness verdict is self-contained.\n  try {\n    const report = checkRegistryCoverage({\n      indexPath: join(REPO, \"registry/index.json\"),\n      sidecarPath: join(REPO, \"registry/tarballs.json\"),\n    });\n    const detail = report.ok\n      ? \"latest/version/pin coverage all green (advertise-follows-upload)\"\n      : `latest: [${report.latest.join(\", \")}] versions: [${report.versions\n          .slice(0, 3)\n          .join(\n            \", \",\n          )}${report.versions.length > 3 ? \", …\" : \"\"}] pins: [${report.pins\n          .slice(0, 3)\n          .join(\", \")}${report.pins.length > 3 ? \", …\" : \"\"}]`;\n    record(\"registry coverage (85/86)\", report.ok, detail);\n  } catch (err) {\n    record(\n      \"registry coverage (85/86)\",\n      false,\n      `coverage check failed to run: ${String(err)}`,\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n// --- 5. R4 audit artifact ------------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst releaseRef = z.string().regex(/^v[0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,100}$/);\nconst auditBindingSchema = z\n  .object({\n    base: releaseRef,\n    tag: releaseRef,\n    reviewed_sha: z.string().regex(/^[a-f0-9]{40}$/),\n  })\n  .strict();\nconst releaseAuditSchema = auditBindingSchema\n  .extend({\n    schema_version: z.literal(2),\n    status: z.literal(\"clean\"),\n    critical: z.literal(0),\n    reviewed_scope: z\n      .array(z.string().trim().min(1).max(512))\n      .min(1)\n      .max(10000),\n    reviewers: z\n      .array(\n        z\n          .object({\n            role: z.enum([\"code_review\", \"security_audit\"]),\n            identity: z.string().trim().min(1).max(200),\n            reviewed_at: z.iso.datetime({ offset: true }),\n          })\n          .strict(),\n      )\n      .length(2)\n      .refine(\n        (reviewers) =>\n          new Set(reviewers.map((reviewer) => reviewer.role)).size === 2,\n        \"Both code review and security audit must be completed\",\n      ),\n  })\n  .strict();\n\nexport type AuditBinding = z.infer<typeof auditBindingSchema>;\n\n// R370: only these two tag-specific files may change after the reviewed commit.\n// No directory-wide docs exemption: a new policy, script or product byte needs review.\nexport const ATTESTATION_ONLY_PATHS = [\n  \"outputs/audit/release-audit-{tag}.md\",\n  \"docs/releases/{tag}-checklist.md\",\n] as const;\n\n/** File-backed boundary: a filename alone is never an R4 attestation. */\nexport function auditArtifactIsValid(\n  path: string,\n  expected: AuditBinding,\n): boolean {\n  try {\n    return auditSourceIsValid(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\"), expected);\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction auditSourceIsValid(source: string, expected: AuditBinding): boolean {\n  try {\n    const binding = auditBindingSchema.parse(expected);\n    const frontmatter = /^---\\r?\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\r?\\n---(?:\\r?\\n|$)/.exec(source);\n    if (!frontmatter || source.length > 1_000_000) return false;\n    const audit = releaseAuditSchema.parse(Bun.YAML.parse(frontmatter[1]!));\n    return (\n      audit.base === binding.base &&\n      audit.tag === binding.tag &&\n      audit.reviewed_sha === binding.reviewed_sha\n    );\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\n/** Read committed bytes, never a working-tree substitute for the tagged attestation. */\nexport function auditSuccessorIsValid(\n  repo: string,\n  tag: string,\n  tagSha: string,\n): boolean {\n  try {\n    releaseRef.parse(tag);\n    z.string()\n      .regex(/^[a-f0-9]{40}$/)\n      .parse(tagSha);\n    const reviewedSha = run(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", `${tagSha}^`], repo);\n    // A merge has several parents and cannot use an ambiguous first-parent review.\n    const parents = run(\n      \"git\",\n      [\"rev-list\", \"--parents\", \"-n\", \"1\", tagSha],\n      repo,\n    ).split(\" \");\n    if (parents.length !== 2 || parents[1] !== reviewedSha) return false;\n    const allowed = ATTESTATION_ONLY_PATHS.map((path) =>\n      path.replace(\"{tag}\", tag),\n    );\n    // Preserve all filename bytes: trimming could turn a leading-space path into an allowed one.\n    const changed = execFileSync(\n      \"git\",\n      [\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--no-renames\", \"-z\", reviewedSha, tagSha],\n      { cwd: repo },\n    )\n      .toString()\n      .split(\"\\0\")\n      .filter(Boolean);\n    if (changed.length === 0 || changed.some((path) => !allowed.includes(path)))\n      return false;\n    const base = run(\n      \"git\",\n      [\"describe\", \"--tags\", \"--abbrev=0\", \"--match\", \"v[0-9]*\", reviewedSha],\n      repo,\n    );\n    const auditPath = allowed[0]!;\n    // A symlink is not an audit/checklist file. Both must exist as regular blobs.\n    for (const path of allowed) {\n      const entry = run(\"git\", [\"ls-tree\", tagSha, \"--\", path], repo);\n      if (!entry.startsWith(\"100644 blob \")) return false;\n    }\n    return auditSourceIsValid(readGitBlob(repo, tagSha, auditPath), {\n      base,\n      tag,\n      reviewed_sha: reviewedSha,\n    });\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction checkAuditArtifact(tag: string, sha: string): void {\n  record(\n    \"R4 release audit on file\",\n    auditSuccessorIsValid(REPO, tag, sha),\n    `requires clean code/security audit of ${sha}^ and only the two ${tag} attestation paths in its successor; CI still binds ${sha}`,\n  );\n}\n\n// --- 6. per-release checklist --------------------------------------------------------------------\nexport function checkChecklist(tag: string, sha: string, repo = REPO): boolean {\n  try {\n    releaseRef.parse(tag);\n    z.string()\n      .regex(/^[a-f0-9]{40}$/)\n      .parse(sha);\n    const path = `docs/releases/${tag}-checklist.md`;\n    const source = readGitBlob(repo, sha, path);\n    const unchecked = (source.match(/^\\s*-\\s\\[\\s\\]/gm) ?? []).length;\n    record(\n      \"per-release checklist\",\n      unchecked === 0,\n      unchecked === 0\n        ? `all boxes checked at ${sha}`\n        : `${String(unchecked)} unchecked box(es) at ${sha}`,\n    );\n    return unchecked === 0;\n  } catch {\n    record(\n      \"per-release checklist\",\n      false,\n      `MISSING or unreadable docs/releases/${tag}-checklist.md at ${sha}`,\n    );\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\n// --- 7. live-hybrid golden leg (--local) ---------------------------------------------------------\nfunction checkLiveHybrid(): void {\n  const key =\n    process.env.CAISSON_DOCS__OPENROUTER_API_KEY ??\n    process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY ??\n    \"\";\n  if (key.length === 0) {\n    record(\n      \"live-hybrid golden leg\",\n      false,\n      \"no OpenRouter key in env — source the env and re-run, or drop --local and attest via the checklist\",\n    );\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    execFileSync(\"bun\", [\"run\", \"test:live\"], {\n      cwd: join(REPO, \"services/docs\"),\n      stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n      env: { ...process.env, OPENROUTER_API_KEY: key },\n      timeout: 15 * 60_000,\n    });\n    record(\n      \"live-hybrid golden leg\",\n      true,\n      \"services/docs test:live green (real fusion path)\",\n    );\n  } catch {\n    record(\"live-hybrid golden leg\", false, \"services/docs test:live FAILED\");\n  }\n}\n\n// Entry point guard (ADR-0414). Everything above is importable; only a direct\n// `bun scripts/release-readiness.ts` runs the gate. Without this, importing the module to test\n// REQUIRED_CHECKS parses argv, prints \"FATAL: --tag is required\", and exits the test process.\n// release-train.yml's R3 job invokes this file directly, so `import.meta.main` is true there.\nif (import.meta.main) {\n  const { tag, sha, local } = parseArgs(Bun.argv.slice(2));\n  console.log(\n    `release-readiness — tag ${tag}, sha ${sha.slice(0, 12)}${local ? \", local\" : \"\"}\\n`,\n  );\n  checkTagOnMain(sha);\n  checkTagSigned(tag);\n  checkCi(sha);\n  checkChangesetsDrained();\n  checkChangelogs();\n  checkSot();\n  checkRegistryCoverageGate();\n  checkAuditArtifact(tag, sha);\n  checkChecklist(tag, sha);\n  if (local) checkLiveHybrid();\n\n  const failed = results.filter((r) => !r.ok);\n  console.log(\n    `\\n${failed.length === 0 ? \"READY\" : \"NOT READY\"} — ${String(results.length - failed.length)}/${String(results.length)} checks green`,\n  );\n  process.exit(failed.length === 0 ? 0 : 1);\n}\n</file>\n\n<file path=\".github/workflows/security-scan.yml\">\nname: security-scan\n# The deterministic security layer (SAST + supply-chain), split into its own workflow per the\n# ci.yml convention. REQUIRED since the ADR-0327 scan-gate flip (sequenced after the CAISSON-95\n# pinning in this same change): `deterministic` joins the required-check set — check ·\n# standards-gate · registry-index · oscal-conformance · deterministic (· support-bot, added by\n# ADR-0414 — see that workflow's header). As with the others,\n# \"required\" is discipline on this free-plan private repo (no enforced branch protection): the\n# convention is enforced by scripts/release-readiness.ts (REQUIRED_CHECKS) and review practice,\n# not a GitHub gate. `semgrep-pro` stays advisory (dormant until its token is provisioned).\n# Runs the repo-local tools/security/scan.sh — the same driver the operator runs locally.\n#\n# Scanner installs are version-pinned + digest-verified against tools/security/versions.env\n# (CAISSON-95) — no curl|sh from a moving main branch, no floating `latest`. The only third-party\n# marketplace action is the SHA-pinned astral-sh/setup-uv (same pin as support-bot.yml). No SARIF\n# upload to the GitHub Security tab — that needs Advanced Security, which this private free-plan\n# repo doesn't have; the SARIF set is saved as a downloadable artifact instead.\n#\n# The Semgrep PRO leg is a separate job gated on the SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN secret (a new external\n# egress sink to semgrep.dev — see identity/security-surfaces.md). It stays dormant until the\n# token is provisioned.\non:\n  schedule:\n    # Daily 06:37 UTC on main; no image publication or registry credentials (R332).\n    - cron: \"37 6 * * *\"\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  pull_request:\n    # Defaults plus ready_for_review — flipping a draft to ready fires the full run (CAISSON-96).\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: \"security-scan-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event_name }}-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.ref }}\"\n  cancel-in-progress: true\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  # Deterministic layer: semgrep floor rules + p/security-audit, ruff flake8-bandit (support-bot),\n  # trivy, osv-scanner, trufflehog (verified-only), Dockerfile digest gate (advisory). SEMGREP_JOBS=1\n  # dodges the semgrep-core io_uring crash the fleet box can hit under parallelism.\n  deterministic:\n    # CAISSON-96 draft guard — drafts skip; the ready_for_review trigger runs the full scan.\n    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    timeout-minutes: 20\n    env:\n      SEMGREP_JOBS: \"1\"\n      SEMGREP_SEND_METRICS: \"off\"\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0 # trufflehog git-history scan needs full history\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@11f9893b081a58869d3b5fccaea48c9e9e46f990 # v8.3.2\n        with:\n          version: \"0.12.2\" # pinned (same pin as support-bot.yml; no drift)\n      - name: base rescan contract tests (offline)\n        run: python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tools/security -p test_*images.py -v\n      - name: runtime OS upgrade contract tests (offline)\n        run: python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tools/security -p test_runtime_os_patch.py -v\n      - name: install scanners (pinned versions, sha256-verified release artifacts)\n        id: scanners\n        run: |\n          # CAISSON-95: every scanner is version-pinned and digest-verified against\n          # tools/security/versions.env — the old `curl | sh` installers fetched their script from\n          # each project's MOVING main branch (an unauditable execution path), and the\n          # `command -v || install` guards would have silently accepted ANY preinstalled version.\n          # Installs are now unconditional (deterministic on a throwaway VM) and fail loud:\n          # pipefail + sha256sum -c mean a bad download or tampered artifact reddens the job.\n          # Every download retries (2026-08-12): a single transient 503 from GitHub's release CDN\n          # reddened this job twice in a row on PR #431, five minutes apart, while all three URLs\n          # served 200 from the operator box — runner-side egress, not the pins. Retrying costs\n          # nothing in integrity: `sha256sum -c` still verifies each artifact against versions.env,\n          # so a retry can only turn a transport failure into the same verified bytes or a red job.\n          set -eo pipefail\n          source tools/security/versions.env\n          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n          mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\n          uv tool install \"semgrep==${SEMGREP_VERSION}\"\n          uv tool install \"ruff==${RUFF_VERSION}\"\n          tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" \"https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/releases/download/v${TRIVY_VERSION}/trivy_${TRIVY_VERSION}_Linux-64bit.tar.gz\"\n          echo \"${TRIVY_SHA256}  $tmp/trivy.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" trivy\n          install -m755 \"$tmp/trivy\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/trivy\"\n          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/trufflehog.tgz\" \"https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/releases/download/v${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}/trufflehog_${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}_linux_amd64.tar.gz\"\n          echo \"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256}  $tmp/trufflehog.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/trufflehog.tgz\" trufflehog\n          install -m755 \"$tmp/trufflehog\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/trufflehog\"\n          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/osv-scanner\" \"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/releases/download/v${OSV_SCANNER_VERSION}/osv-scanner_linux_amd64\"\n          echo \"${OSV_SCANNER_SHA256}  $tmp/osv-scanner\" | sha256sum -c -\n          install -m755 \"$tmp/osv-scanner\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/osv-scanner\"\n          rm -rf \"$tmp\"\n          # Re-assert every tool resolved — a missing tool must hard-fail the job, never silent-skip.\n          for t in semgrep ruff trivy trufflehog osv-scanner; do\n            command -v \"$t\" >/dev/null || { echo \"::error::$t missing after install — scan layer would silently skip\"; exit 1; }\n          done\n      - name: security scan (SAST + supply-chain)\n        run: |\n          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n          # SARIF lands in $RUNNER_TEMP (OUT of the scanned tree) so `trivy fs .` never re-scans\n          # semgrep's freshly-written SARIF. Set at step scope: the `runner` context is unavailable\n          # in a job-level `env:`, and $RUNNER_TEMP is the shell form of it inside a step. The dir is\n          # deliberately NON-hidden: actions/upload-artifact@v4 (>=4.4) excludes hidden files/dirs by\n          # default, so a dot-dir uploaded empty (\"No files were found\") — the SARIF set evaporated.\n          export SECURITY_OUT_DIR=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/security-out\"\n          # --strict-digests: Dockerfile digest-pin check (K-03) is ENFORCING — the ADR-0315\n          # trigger (Renovate's first pin-wave merged) fired 2026-07-13; check-docker-digests.sh\n          # proven green on main 2026-07-17 before the flip.\n          bash tools/security/scan.sh --layer ci --strict-digests\n      - name: report raw Dockerfile base digests (informational, anonymous)\n        if: ${{ !cancelled() && steps.scanners.outcome == 'success' }}\n        continue-on-error: true # R335: raw-base results never gate the job.\n        run: |\n          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n          python3 tools/security/rescan_base_images.py --output \"$RUNNER_TEMP/security-out\"\n      - name: upload SARIF artifacts\n        if: always()\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a # v7\n        with:\n          name: security-sarif-${{ github.sha }}\n          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/security-out\n          if-no-files-found: warn\n          retention-days: 30\n\n  # R359 / CR-05: one stable check consumes every matrix member's result, including\n  # cancellation/failure/skips. always() prevents a red dependency from skipping the gate.\n  runtime-images-gate:\n    name: runtime-images-gate\n    if: always()\n    needs: [runtime-select, runtime-images]\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    timeout-minutes: 5\n    steps:\n      - name: require successful runtime selection and every image\n        env:\n          SELECT_RESULT: ${{ needs.runtime-select.result }}\n          MATRIX_RESULT: ${{ needs.runtime-images.result }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          test \"$SELECT_RESULT\" = success\n          test \"$MATRIX_RESULT\" = success\n\n  # Semgrep PRO (interfile / cross-function taint). Dormant until SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN is set. The job\n  # ALWAYS runs — a job-level `if` CANNOT reference the `secrets` context (doing so is a parse-time\n  # \"Unrecognized named-value: secrets\" that invalidates the ENTIRE workflow file, killing the\n  # deterministic job too) — but the single step below no-ops without a token. `semgrep ci`\n  # self-authenticates from the token and pulls the org policy rules. SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN and\n  # SEMGREP_RULES are mutually exclusive — never set both.\n  semgrep-pro:\n    # CAISSON-96 draft guard — drafts skip; the ready_for_review trigger runs the full scan.\n    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    # 45, not 20: this job's runtime swings hard. On 2026-07-27 it hit the old 20-minute ceiling on\n    # `87202cd9` and then passed in ~3 minutes on an immediate re-run of the identical tree — a 7x\n    # spread. A timed-out job reports as `cancelled`, which reads like someone aborted it rather\n    # than a scan that never finished, and because this check is advisory nothing forced anyone to\n    # look. The ceiling now sits above the observed worst case so the result means something.\n    #\n    # NOT changed here: the `-j 1` below (and its SEMGREP_JOBS twin). Single-threading is a\n    # deliberate workaround for a semgrep-core io_uring crash, and that comment was written about\n    # the self-hosted fleet box — this job runs on a 4-vCPU Blacksmith VM, so the workaround may not\n    # apply and is likely the bulk of the runtime. Worth testing, but not worth guessing at inside a\n    # launch deploy: removing a crash workaround on inference is how you trade a slow check for a\n    # flaky one.\n    timeout-minutes: 45\n    env:\n      SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN }}\n      SEMGREP_JOBS: \"1\"\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n      - uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@11f9893b081a58869d3b5fccaea48c9e9e46f990 # v8.3.2\n        with:\n          version: \"0.12.2\" # pinned (same pin as support-bot.yml; no drift)\n      # One guarded step: skip cleanly (installing nothing) when the token is absent; otherwise\n      # install the PINNED semgrep (CAISSON-95, tools/security/versions.env) and run the Pro\n      # platform-policy scan (interfile/cross-function taint). The custom floor rules run in the\n      # `deterministic` job (pattern rules need no Pro engine); add them to the Semgrep policy to\n      # have them Pro-analyzed too.\n      - name: semgrep ci (Pro cross-file taint) — dormant until SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN is set\n        run: |\n          if [ -z \"${SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN:-}\" ]; then\n            echo \"SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN not set — Pro scan skipped (provision the repo secret to activate)\"\n            exit 0\n          fi\n          set -eo pipefail\n          source tools/security/versions.env\n          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n          uv tool install \"semgrep==${SEMGREP_VERSION}\"\n          semgrep ci -j 1\n\n  # zizmor — GitHub Actions workflow auditor (Kickoff T task 2). ADVISORY for now: SARIF mode\n  # always exits 0 (findings live in the SARIF, not the exit code), so this job can never block\n  # a merge. Gate ramp: once the finding set is triaged to zero-or-ignored (zizmor.yml `ignore`\n  # entries with rationale), drop `--no-exit-codes`, switch --format to plain, and add the job to\n  # the required-check convention in scripts/release-readiness.ts — the repo is already SHA-pinned\n  # throughout, so the steady-state finding rate should be near zero. Same pinned-install\n  # discipline as the deterministic job: version + sha256 from tools/security/versions.env\n  # (zizmor releases attach no checksums file — the pinned digest was verified by local download,\n  # see versions.env comment).\n  zizmor:\n    # CAISSON-96 draft guard — drafts skip; the ready_for_review trigger runs the full scan.\n    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n      - name: install zizmor (pinned version, sha256-verified release artifact)\n        run: |\n          set -eo pipefail\n          source tools/security/versions.env\n          mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\n          tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/zizmor.tgz\" \"https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/releases/download/v${ZIZMOR_VERSION}/zizmor-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz\"\n          echo \"${ZIZMOR_SHA256}  $tmp/zizmor.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/zizmor.tgz\"\n          find \"$tmp\" -name zizmor -type f -exec install -m755 {} \"$HOME/.local/bin/zizmor\" \\;\n          rm -rf \"$tmp\"\n          command -v \"$HOME/.local/bin/zizmor\" >/dev/null || { echo \"::error::zizmor missing after install\"; exit 1; }\n      - name: zizmor audit (advisory — SARIF artifact, never blocks)\n        env:\n          # Online audits (impostor-commit, ref-confusion, stale-action-refs) need read access to\n          # public commit graphs; the default token's `contents: read` suffices.\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n        run: |\n          export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n          mkdir -p \"$RUNNER_TEMP/zizmor-out\"\n          zizmor --persona=regular --format=sarif --no-exit-codes .github/workflows/ > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/zizmor-out/zizmor.sarif\"\n          # Human-readable echo for the job log (advisory visibility without downloading the SARIF).\n          zizmor --persona=regular --no-exit-codes .github/workflows/ || true\n      - name: upload zizmor SARIF artifact\n        if: always()\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a # v7\n        with:\n          name: zizmor-sarif-${{ github.sha }}\n          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/zizmor-out\n          if-no-files-found: warn\n          retention-days: 30\n\n  runtime-select:\n    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.draft == false\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    outputs:\n      matrix: ${{ steps.select.outputs.matrix }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - id: select\n        run: |\n          matrix=\"$(python3 -B tools/security/rescan_runtime_images.py --matrix)\"\n          printf 'matrix=%s\\n' \"$matrix\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n  runtime-images:\n    name: runtime image (${{ matrix.name }})\n    needs: runtime-select\n    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    timeout-minutes: 35\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      max-parallel: 4\n      matrix: ${{ fromJSON(needs.runtime-select.outputs.matrix) }}\n    env:\n      IMAGE: caisson-runtime-rescan:${{ matrix.name }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n      - name: prepare disposable runner disk\n        run: |\n          # Same fixed SDK set proven by PR 483. This job needs its own cleanup\n          # before that sibling PR merges; neither PR may merge independently (R336).\n          df -B1 / \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          sudo rm -rf -- /usr/local/lib/android /usr/local/.ghcup /usr/local/swift /usr/share/dotnet\n          df -B1 / \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n      - name: install pinned Trivy\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          source tools/security/versions.env\n          tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n          curl -sSfL --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 --retry-all-errors -o \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" \"https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/releases/download/v${TRIVY_VERSION}/trivy_${TRIVY_VERSION}_Linux-64bit.tar.gz\"\n          echo \"${TRIVY_SHA256}  $tmp/trivy.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -\n          tar -C \"$tmp\" -xzf \"$tmp/trivy.tgz\" trivy\n          mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\n          install -m755 \"$tmp/trivy\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/trivy\"\n          echo \"$HOME/.local/bin\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@37fe631027851001ddb9b187196cc803df7f5f0e # v4.3.0\n      - name: build patched runtime (no publish)\n        uses: docker/build-push-action@53b7df96c91f9c12dcc8a07bcb9ccacbed38856a # v7.3.0\n        with:\n          context: ${{ matrix.context }}\n          file: ${{ matrix.dockerfile }}\n          target: ${{ matrix.target }}\n          platforms: linux/amd64\n          no-cache: true # Execute apt update/upgrade on every scheduled rebuild.\n          pull: true\n          push: false\n          load: true\n          tags: ${{ env.IMAGE }}\n      - name: record built image provenance\n        env:\n          DOCKERFILE: ${{ matrix.dockerfile }}\n          TARGET: ${{ matrix.target }}\n        run: |\n          mkdir -p \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan\"\n          git rev-parse HEAD > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/source-sha.txt\"\n          printf '%s\\n' \"$DOCKERFILE\" \"$TARGET\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/build-target.txt\"\n          docker image inspect \"$IMAGE\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/image-inspect.json\"\n          df -B1 / \"$RUNNER_TEMP\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/disk-before.txt\"\n      - name: enforce runtime OS vulnerabilities and report application residual\n        run: python3 -B tools/security/rescan_runtime_images.py --image \"$IMAGE\" --output \"$RUNNER_TEMP/runtime-scan/image.json\"\n      - name: upload runtime reports and application/unfixed residuals\n        if: always()\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a # v7\n        with:\n          name: runtime-rescan-${{ matrix.name }}\n          path: ${{ runner.temp }}/runtime-scan\n          if-no-files-found: error\n          retention-days: 30\n</file>\n\n</files>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba scripts/release-readiness.ts'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba scripts/release-readiness.ts'","aggregated_output":"     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bun\n     2\t/**\n     3\t * release-readiness.ts — the ADR-0318 R3 gate. Every check must be GREEN before the release\n     4\t * train's propagation legs run; any red exits nonzero and the train stops before touching an\n     5\t * external surface. Run by .github/workflows/release-train.yml on the release SHA, and locally:\n     6\t *\n     7\t *   bun scripts/release-readiness.ts --tag v2026.07.30 [--sha <sha>] [--local]\n     8\t *\n     9\t * Checks (R3, locked; #0 added by ADR-0325):\n    10\t *   0. Release SHA on main — the tag targets a commit that is an ancestor of origin/main (the\n    11\t *      merged version-PR commit; a tag cut on a stray branch must never train).\n    12\t *   0b. Release tag signed (ADR-0382) — `git tag -v` verifies the tag against the allowed-signers\n    13\t *      file. ADVISORY for now: tags cut before the lock are unsigned and cannot become signed.\n    14\t *   1. CI green on the release SHA — all seven required checks, including the source security\n    15\t *      layer, support-bot and the R359 runtime-images-gate aggregate, completed successfully.\n    16\t *   2. Changesets drained — no pending .changeset/*.md (the version PR consumed them —\n    17\t *      version-pr.yml, ADR-0325; never a feature-branch or tag-path act).\n    18\t *   3. CHANGELOGs written — every non-private workspace package's CHANGELOG.md leads with its\n    19\t *      package.json version.\n    20\t *   4. `bun run sot` green — the SoT drift tool (ADR-ceiling parity, frontmatter/docs freshness,\n    21\t *      archive integrity, tracker-vs-PR reality, changeset preflight). Doubles as the R3\n    22\t *      docs-freshness check.\n    23\t *   4b. Registry coverage invariants (CAISSON-85/86) — every module's `latest` has a tarball row\n    24\t *      (hard), no advertised version outside the frozen pre-sidecar backlog is rowless, and every\n    25\t *      served member pin resolves served+tarball-backed (advertise-follows-upload, static half).\n    26\t *   5. R4 audit artifact on file — outputs/audit/release-audit-<tag>.md (the fresh full\n    27\t *      SHIP-audit-lane review of the cumulative diff since the last release tag).\n    28\t *   6. Per-release checklist complete — docs/releases/<tag>-checklist.md exists with ZERO\n    29\t *      unchecked boxes (the human items: marketing surfaces, announcement, live-leg attestations).\n    30\t *   7. (--local only) the live-hybrid retrieval golden leg — services/docs `bun run test:live`\n    31\t *      with real keys (Kickoff-M picker 2026-07-10: this leg gates at release readiness, not PR\n    32\t *      CI). In the train (no keys) the checklist attestation (#6) carries it instead.\n    33\t */\n    34\timport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\n    35\timport { existsSync, readdirSync, readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n    36\timport { join, resolve } from \"node:path\";\n    37\timport { z } from \"zod\";\n    38\timport { checkRegistryCoverage } from \"../registry/scripts/coverage-invariants\";\n    39\t\n    40\tconst REPO = resolve(import.meta.dir, \"..\");\n    41\texport const REQUIRED_CHECKS = [\n    42\t  \"check\",\n    43\t  \"standards-gate\",\n    44\t  \"registry-index\",\n    45\t  \"oscal-conformance\",\n    46\t  // ADR-0327 scan-gate flip (CAISSON-95): the deterministic security layer joins the required\n    47\t  // set once its installers are pinned — which landed in the same change as this line.\n    48\t  \"deterministic\",\n    49\t  // ADR-0414: the Python gate for services/support-bot, promoted out of advisory in the same\n    50\t  // change that gave that service an automated Railway deploy. Its paths filter was removed in\n    51\t  // the same commit — this list treats a check that never reported as `missing`, so a\n    52\t  // path-scoped required check would red readiness on every release that did not touch the bot.\n    53\t  \"support-bot\",\n    54\t  // R359 / CR-05: source scans cannot stand in for the enforcing runtime-image matrix.\n    55\t  \"runtime-images-gate\",\n    56\t] as const;\n    57\t\n    58\tinterface Args {\n    59\t  tag: string;\n    60\t  sha: string;\n    61\t  local: boolean;\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\tfunction parseArgs(argv: readonly string[]): Args {\n    65\t  let tag = \"\";\n    66\t  let sha = \"\";\n    67\t  let local = false;\n    68\t  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {\n    69\t    const a = argv[i];\n    70\t    if (a === \"--tag\") tag = argv[++i] ?? \"\";\n    71\t    else if (a === \"--sha\") sha = argv[++i] ?? \"\";\n    72\t    else if (a === \"--local\") local = true;\n    73\t  }\n    74\t  if (!tag) {\n    75\t    console.error(\"FATAL: --tag <release-tag> is required\");\n    76\t    process.exit(1);\n    77\t  }\n    78\t  if (!sha) {\n    79\t    sha = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], { cwd: REPO })\n    80\t      .toString()\n    81\t      .trim();\n    82\t  }\n    83\t  return { tag, sha, local };\n    84\t}\n    85\t\n    86\ttype CheckResult = { name: string; ok: boolean; detail: string };\n    87\tconst results: CheckResult[] = [];\n    88\tfunction record(name: string, ok: boolean, detail: string): void {\n    89\t  results.push({ name, ok, detail });\n    90\t  console.log(`${ok ? \"  ✓\" : \"  ✗\"} ${name} — ${detail}`);\n    91\t}\n    92\t\n    93\tfunction run(cmd: string, args: readonly string[], cwd = REPO): string {\n    94\t  return execFileSync(cmd, [...args], {\n    95\t    cwd,\n    96\t    stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n    97\t  })\n    98\t    .toString()\n    99\t    .trim();\n   100\t}\n   101\t\n   102\t/** Blob contents are parser input: preserve every byte, including leading whitespace. */\n   103\tfunction readGitBlob(repo: string, sha: string, path: string): string {\n   104\t  return execFileSync(\"git\", [\"show\", `${sha}:${path}`], {\n   105\t    cwd: repo,\n   106\t    stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n   107\t  }).toString(\"utf8\");\n   108\t}\n   109\t\n   110\t// --- 0. release SHA on main (ADR-0325) -----------------------------------------------------------\n   111\tfunction checkTagOnMain(sha: string): void {\n   112\t  try {\n   113\t    // In CI the checkout is at the tag with full history; locally origin/main may be stale —\n   114\t    // refresh it quietly, tolerating offline runs (merge-base still answers from local refs).\n   115\t    try {\n   116\t      run(\"git\", [\"fetch\", \"origin\", \"main\", \"--quiet\"]);\n   117\t    } catch {\n   118\t      /* offline — check against the local origin/main ref */\n   119\t    }\n   120\t    run(\"git\", [\"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", sha, \"origin/main\"]);\n   121\t    record(\n   122\t      \"release SHA on main\",\n   123\t      true,\n   124\t      `${sha.slice(0, 8)} is an ancestor of origin/main`,\n   125\t    );\n   126\t  } catch {\n   127\t    record(\n   128\t      \"release SHA on main\",\n   129\t      false,\n   130\t      `${sha.slice(0, 8)} is NOT on origin/main — the tag must target the merged version-PR commit`,\n   131\t    );\n   132\t  }\n   133\t}\n   134\t\n   135\t// --- 0b. release tag is signed (ADR-0382) -------------------------------------------------------\n   136\t// An annotated tag says WHO claims a release; a signed one proves it. Without a signature anyone\n   137\t// with push access can move or forge a tag onto a different commit and every downstream leg — the\n   138\t// registry publish, the mirror sync, the fleet redeploy — trusts it, because each of them resolves\n   139\t// the tag rather than a SHA. `git tag -v` verifies against the allowed-signers file; it fails on an\n   140\t// unsigned tag, an unknown signer, and a signature that does not match the tag's bytes.\n   141\t//\n   142\t// Tags cut before the signing lock are unsigned and cannot retroactively become signed, so this is\n   143\t// a WARNING here rather than a hard gate: it reports honestly on every release without failing the\n   144\t// train on history it cannot change. Promote it to a blocking check once the first signed tag has\n   145\t// trained end to end (that flip is a one-word change: `record(..., ok, ...)`).\n   146\tfunction checkTagSigned(tag: string): void {\n   147\t  try {\n   148\t    run(\"git\", [\"tag\", \"-v\", tag]);\n   149\t    record(\"release tag signed\", true, `${tag} carries a valid signature`);\n   150\t  } catch {\n   151\t    // Not fatal — see above. Surfaced so an unsigned tag is a visible choice, never an oversight.\n   152\t    console.log(\n   153\t      `  ! release tag signed — ${tag} is UNSIGNED or its signer is not in the allowed-signers file (advisory; see docs/ops/release-tag-signing.md)`,\n   154\t    );\n   155\t  }\n   156\t}\n   157\t\n   158\t// --- 1. CI green on the release SHA -------------------------------------------------------------\n   159\tfunction checkCi(sha: string): void {\n   160\t  try {\n   161\t    const raw = run(\"gh\", [\n   162\t      \"api\",\n   163\t      `repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/${sha}/check-runs`,\n   164\t      \"--paginate\",\n   165\t      \"-q\",\n   166\t      \"[.check_runs[] | {name, status, conclusion}]\",\n   167\t    ]);\n   168\t    // --paginate emits one JSON array per page; normalize to a single list.\n   169\t    const runs = raw\n   170\t      .split(\"\\n\")\n   171\t      .filter(Boolean)\n   172\t      .flatMap(\n   173\t        (line) =>\n   174\t          JSON.parse(line) as {\n   175\t            name: string;\n   176\t            status: string;\n   177\t            conclusion: string | null;\n   178\t          }[],\n   179\t      );\n   180\t    const missing: string[] = [];\n   181\t    const red: string[] = [];\n   182\t    for (const required of REQUIRED_CHECKS) {\n   183\t      const match = runs.filter((r) => r.name === required);\n   184\t      if (match.length === 0) {\n   185\t        missing.push(required);\n   186\t        continue;\n   187\t      }\n   188\t      // A check re-run replaces its predecessor in the API answer set; any green instance passes.\n   189\t      if (\n   190\t        !match.some(\n   191\t          (r) => r.status === \"completed\" && r.conclusion === \"success\",\n   192\t        )\n   193\t      )\n   194\t        red.push(required);\n   195\t    }\n   196\t    const ok = missing.length === 0 && red.length === 0;\n   197\t    record(\n   198\t      \"CI green on release SHA\",\n   199\t      ok,\n   200\t      ok\n   201\t        ? `all ${String(REQUIRED_CHECKS.length)} required checks green at ${sha.slice(0, 8)}`\n   202\t        : `missing: [${missing.join(\", \")}] red: [${red.join(\", \")}]`,\n   203\t    );\n   204\t  } catch (err) {\n   205\t    record(\"CI green on release SHA\", false, `gh api failed: ${String(err)}`);\n   206\t  }\n   207\t}\n   208\t\n   209\t// --- 2. changesets drained -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n   210\tfunction checkChangesetsDrained(): void {\n   211\t  const pending = readdirSync(join(REPO, \".changeset\")).filter(\n   212\t    (f) => f.endsWith(\".md\") && f !== \"README.md\",\n   213\t  );\n   214\t  record(\n   215\t    \"changesets drained\",\n   216\t    pending.length === 0,\n   217\t    pending.length === 0\n   218\t      ? \"no pending changesets\"\n   219\t      : `${String(pending.length)} pending (version cut not consumed): ${pending.slice(0, 5).join(\", \")}${pending.length > 5 ? \", …\" : \"\"}`,\n   220\t  );\n   221\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t// --- 3. CHANGELOGs written -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n   224\tfunction checkChangelogs(): void {\n   225\t  const bad: string[] = [];\n   226\t  for (const group of [\"packages\", \"tooling\"]) {\n   227\t    const base = join(REPO, group);\n   228\t    if (!existsSync(base)) continue;\n   229\t    for (const slug of readdirSync(base)) {\n   230\t      const pj = join(base, slug, \"package.json\");\n   231\t      if (!existsSync(pj)) continue;\n   232\t      const pkg = JSON.parse(readFileSync(pj, \"utf8\")) as {\n   233\t        name: string;\n   234\t        version?: string;\n   235\t        private?: boolean;\n   236\t      };\n   237\t      if (pkg.private || !pkg.version) continue;\n   238\t      const changelog = join(base, slug, \"CHANGELOG.md\");\n   239\t      if (!existsSync(changelog)) {\n   240\t        bad.push(`${pkg.name} (no CHANGELOG.md)`);\n   241\t        continue;\n   242\t      }\n   243\t      if (!readFileSync(changelog, \"utf8\").includes(`## ${pkg.version}`))\n   244\t        bad.push(`${pkg.name} (no ## ${pkg.version} entry)`);\n   245\t    }\n   246\t  }\n   247\t  record(\n   248\t    \"CHANGELOGs written\",\n   249\t    bad.length === 0,\n   250\t    bad.length === 0\n   251\t      ? \"every versioned package's CHANGELOG leads with its current version\"\n   252\t      : bad.slice(0, 5).join(\"; \") + (bad.length > 5 ? \"; …\" : \"\"),\n   253\t  );\n   254\t}\n   255\t\n   256\t// --- 4. sot green (doubles as docs freshness) ----------------------------------------------------\n   257\tfunction checkSot(): void {\n   258\t  try {\n   259\t    run(\"bun\", [\"run\", \"sot\"]);\n   260\t    record(\"bun run sot\", true, \"SoT drift tool green (incl. docs freshness)\");\n   261\t  } catch (err) {\n   262\t    // Surface the captured drift report — a CI readiness red must not be blind (first ride:\n   263\t    // the only failure signal was this one-liner while sot's own output was swallowed).\n   264\t    const e = err as { stdout?: Buffer | string; stderr?: Buffer | string };\n   265\t    for (const chunk of [e.stdout, e.stderr]) {\n   266\t      const text = chunk?.toString().trim();\n   267\t      if (text) console.error(text);\n   268\t    }\n   269\t    record(\"bun run sot\", false, \"sot check failed — drift report above\");\n   270\t  }\n   271\t}\n   272\t\n   273\t// --- 4b. registry coverage invariants (CAISSON-85/86) --------------------------------------------\n   274\tfunction checkRegistryCoverageGate(): void {\n   275\t  // Static advertise-follows-upload proof: every module's latest has a tarball row (hard), no\n   276\t  // advertised version outside the frozen pre-sidecar backlog is rowless, and every served member\n   277\t  // pin resolves served+tarball-backed. Same invariants the registry-index CI job enforces via\n   278\t  // coverage-invariants.test.ts — re-run here so the train's readiness verdict is self-contained.\n   279\t  try {\n   280\t    const report = checkRegistryCoverage({\n   281\t      indexPath: join(REPO, \"registry/index.json\"),\n   282\t      sidecarPath: join(REPO, \"registry/tarballs.json\"),\n   283\t    });\n   284\t    const detail = report.ok\n   285\t      ? \"latest/version/pin coverage all green (advertise-follows-upload)\"\n   286\t      : `latest: [${report.latest.join(\", \")}] versions: [${report.versions\n   287\t          .slice(0, 3)\n   288\t          .join(\n   289\t            \", \",\n   290\t          )}${report.versions.length > 3 ? \", …\" : \"\"}] pins: [${report.pins\n   291\t          .slice(0, 3)\n   292\t          .join(\", \")}${report.pins.length > 3 ? \", …\" : \"\"}]`;\n   293\t    record(\"registry coverage (85/86)\", report.ok, detail);\n   294\t  } catch (err) {\n   295\t    record(\n   296\t      \"registry coverage (85/86)\",\n   297\t      false,\n   298\t      `coverage check failed to run: ${String(err)}`,\n   299\t    );\n   300\t  }\n   301\t}\n   302\t\n   303\t// --- 5. R4 audit artifact ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   304\tconst releaseRef = z.string().regex(/^v[0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,100}$/);\n   305\tconst auditBindingSchema = z\n   306\t  .object({\n   307\t    base: releaseRef,\n   308\t    tag: releaseRef,\n   309\t    reviewed_sha: z.string().regex(/^[a-f0-9]{40}$/),\n   310\t  })\n   311\t  .strict();\n   312\tconst releaseAuditSchema = auditBindingSchema\n   313\t  .extend({\n   314\t    schema_version: z.literal(2),\n   315\t    status: z.literal(\"clean\"),\n   316\t    critical: z.literal(0),\n   317\t    reviewed_scope: z\n   318\t      .array(z.string().trim().min(1).max(512))\n   319\t      .min(1)\n   320\t      .max(10000),\n   321\t    reviewers: z\n   322\t      .array(\n   323\t        z\n   324\t          .object({\n   325\t            role: z.enum([\"code_review\", \"security_audit\"]),\n   326\t            identity: z.string().trim().min(1).max(200),\n   327\t            reviewed_at: z.iso.datetime({ offset: true }),\n   328\t          })\n   329\t          .strict(),\n   330\t      )\n   331\t      .length(2)\n   332\t      .refine(\n   333\t        (reviewers) =>\n   334\t          new Set(reviewers.map((reviewer) => reviewer.role)).size === 2,\n   335\t        \"Both code review and security audit must be completed\",\n   336\t      ),\n   337\t  })\n   338\t  .strict();\n   339\t\n   340\texport type AuditBinding = z.infer<typeof auditBindingSchema>;\n   341\t\n   342\t// R370: only these two tag-specific files may change after the reviewed commit.\n   343\t// No directory-wide docs exemption: a new policy, script or product byte needs review.\n   344\texport const ATTESTATION_ONLY_PATHS = [\n   345\t  \"outputs/audit/release-audit-{tag}.md\",\n   346\t  \"docs/releases/{tag}-checklist.md\",\n   347\t] as const;\n   348\t\n   349\t/** File-backed boundary: a filename alone is never an R4 attestation. */\n   350\texport function auditArtifactIsValid(\n   351\t  path: string,\n   352\t  expected: AuditBinding,\n   353\t): boolean {\n   354\t  try {\n   355\t    return auditSourceIsValid(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\"), expected);\n   356\t  } catch {\n   357\t    return false;\n   358\t  }\n   359\t}\n   360\t\n   361\tfunction auditSourceIsValid(source: string, expected: AuditBinding): boolean {\n   362\t  try {\n   363\t    const binding = auditBindingSchema.parse(expected);\n   364\t    const frontmatter = /^---\\r?\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\r?\\n---(?:\\r?\\n|$)/.exec(source);\n   365\t    if (!frontmatter || source.length > 1_000_000) return false;\n   366\t    const audit = releaseAuditSchema.parse(Bun.YAML.parse(frontmatter[1]!));\n   367\t    return (\n   368\t      audit.base === binding.base &&\n   369\t      audit.tag === binding.tag &&\n   370\t      audit.reviewed_sha === binding.reviewed_sha\n   371\t    );\n   372\t  } catch {\n   373\t    return false;\n   374\t  }\n   375\t}\n   376\t\n   377\t/** Read committed bytes, never a working-tree substitute for the tagged attestation. */\n   378\texport function auditSuccessorIsValid(\n   379\t  repo: string,\n   380\t  tag: string,\n   381\t  tagSha: string,\n   382\t): boolean {\n   383\t  try {\n   384\t    releaseRef.parse(tag);\n   385\t    z.string()\n   386\t      .regex(/^[a-f0-9]{40}$/)\n   387\t      .parse(tagSha);\n   388\t    const reviewedSha = run(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", `${tagSha}^`], repo);\n   389\t    // A merge has several parents and cannot use an ambiguous first-parent review.\n   390\t    const parents = run(\n   391\t      \"git\",\n   392\t      [\"rev-list\", \"--parents\", \"-n\", \"1\", tagSha],\n   393\t      repo,\n   394\t    ).split(\" \");\n   395\t    if (parents.length !== 2 || parents[1] !== reviewedSha) return false;\n   396\t    const allowed = ATTESTATION_ONLY_PATHS.map((path) =>\n   397\t      path.replace(\"{tag}\", tag),\n   398\t    );\n   399\t    // Preserve all filename bytes: trimming could turn a leading-space path into an allowed one.\n   400\t    const changed = execFileSync(\n   401\t      \"git\",\n   402\t      [\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--no-renames\", \"-z\", reviewedSha, tagSha],\n   403\t      { cwd: repo },\n   404\t    )\n   405\t      .toString()\n   406\t      .split(\"\\0\")\n   407\t      .filter(Boolean);\n   408\t    if (changed.length === 0 || changed.some((path) => !allowed.includes(path)))\n   409\t      return false;\n   410\t    const base = run(\n   411\t      \"git\",\n   412\t      [\"describe\", \"--tags\", \"--abbrev=0\", \"--match\", \"v[0-9]*\", reviewedSha],\n   413\t      repo,\n   414\t    );\n   415\t    const auditPath = allowed[0]!;\n   416\t    // A symlink is not an audit/checklist file. Both must exist as regular blobs.\n   417\t    for (const path of allowed) {\n   418\t      const entry = run(\"git\", [\"ls-tree\", tagSha, \"--\", path], repo);\n   419\t      if (!entry.startsWith(\"100644 blob \")) return false;\n   420\t    }\n   421\t    return auditSourceIsValid(readGitBlob(repo, tagSha, auditPath), {\n   422\t      base,\n   423\t      tag,\n   424\t      reviewed_sha: reviewedSha,\n   425\t    });\n   426\t  } catch {\n   427\t    return false;\n   428\t  }\n   429\t}\n   430\t\n   431\tfunction checkAuditArtifact(tag: string, sha: string): void {\n   432\t  record(\n   433\t    \"R4 release audit on file\",\n   434\t    auditSuccessorIsValid(REPO, tag, sha),\n   435\t    `requires clean code/security audit of ${sha}^ and only the two ${tag} attestation paths in its successor; CI still binds ${sha}`,\n   436\t  );\n   437\t}\n   438\t\n   439\t// --- 6. per-release checklist --------------------------------------------------------------------\n   440\texport function checkChecklist(tag: string, sha: string, repo = REPO): boolean {\n   441\t  try {\n   442\t    releaseRef.parse(tag);\n   443\t    z.string()\n   444\t      .regex(/^[a-f0-9]{40}$/)\n   445\t      .parse(sha);\n   446\t    const path = `docs/releases/${tag}-checklist.md`;\n   447\t    const source = readGitBlob(repo, sha, path);\n   448\t    const unchecked = (source.match(/^\\s*-\\s\\[\\s\\]/gm) ?? []).length;\n   449\t    record(\n   450\t      \"per-release checklist\",\n   451\t      unchecked === 0,\n   452\t      unchecked === 0\n   453\t        ? `all boxes checked at ${sha}`\n   454\t        : `${String(unchecked)} unchecked box(es) at ${sha}`,\n   455\t    );\n   456\t    return unchecked === 0;\n   457\t  } catch {\n   458\t    record(\n   459\t      \"per-release checklist\",\n   460\t      false,\n   461\t      `MISSING or unreadable docs/releases/${tag}-checklist.md at ${sha}`,\n   462\t    );\n   463\t    return false;\n   464\t  }\n   465\t}\n   466\t\n   467\t// --- 7. live-hybrid golden leg (--local) ---------------------------------------------------------\n   468\tfunction checkLiveHybrid(): void {\n   469\t  const key =\n   470\t    process.env.CAISSON_DOCS__OPENROUTER_API_KEY ??\n   471\t    process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY ??\n   472\t    \"\";\n   473\t  if (key.length === 0) {\n   474\t    record(\n   475\t      \"live-hybrid golden leg\",\n   476\t      false,\n   477\t      \"no OpenRouter key in env — source the env and re-run, or drop --local and attest via the checklist\",\n   478\t    );\n   479\t    return;\n   480\t  }\n   481\t  try {\n   482\t    execFileSync(\"bun\", [\"run\", \"test:live\"], {\n   483\t      cwd: join(REPO, \"services/docs\"),\n   484\t      stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n   485\t      env: { ...process.env, OPENROUTER_API_KEY: key },\n   486\t      timeout: 15 * 60_000,\n   487\t    });\n   488\t    record(\n   489\t      \"live-hybrid golden leg\",\n   490\t      true,\n   491\t      \"services/docs test:live green (real fusion path)\",\n   492\t    );\n   493\t  } catch {\n   494\t    record(\"live-hybrid golden leg\", false, \"services/docs test:live FAILED\");\n   495\t  }\n   496\t}\n   497\t\n   498\t// Entry point guard (ADR-0414). Everything above is importable; only a direct\n   499\t// `bun scripts/release-readiness.ts` runs the gate. Without this, importing the module to test\n   500\t// REQUIRED_CHECKS parses argv, prints \"FATAL: --tag is required\", and exits the test process.\n   501\t// release-train.yml's R3 job invokes this file directly, so `import.meta.main` is true there.\n   502\tif (import.meta.main) {\n   503\t  const { tag, sha, local } = parseArgs(Bun.argv.slice(2));\n   504\t  console.log(\n   505\t    `release-readiness — tag ${tag}, sha ${sha.slice(0, 12)}${local ? \", local\" : \"\"}\\n`,\n   506\t  );\n   507\t  checkTagOnMain(sha);\n   508\t  checkTagSigned(tag);\n   509\t  checkCi(sha);\n   510\t  checkChangesetsDrained();\n   511\t  checkChangelogs();\n   512\t  checkSot();\n   513\t  checkRegistryCoverageGate();\n   514\t  checkAuditArtifact(tag, sha);\n   515\t  checkChecklist(tag, sha);\n   516\t  if (local) checkLiveHybrid();\n   517\t\n   518\t  const failed = results.filter((r) => !r.ok);\n   519\t  console.log(\n   520\t    `\\n${failed.length === 0 ? \"READY\" : \"NOT READY\"} — ${String(results.length - failed.length)}/${String(results.length)} checks green`,\n   521\t  );\n   522\t  process.exit(failed.length === 0 ? 0 : 1);\n   523\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
